write('DATA_SOURCE_OF_TRUTH_AND_MAPPING','Data source of truth and mapping',
 '## Logical target ownership\n\nThe following is a proposed logical data architecture. It does not add, rename or migrate any collection in this phase. Persisted paths and schema versions must be designed with compatible readers and an approved migration plan.\n\n'+table(['Authority','Identity / important fields','Read scope','Source-of-truth rule'],sources)+
 '\n## Command/read flow\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  User[Explicit user action] --> UI[Typed draft + accessible pending state]\n  UI --> Validation[Shared input validation]\n  Validation --> Command[Authorized command: actor + idempotency key + version]\n  Command --> Rules[Trusted business authorization and storage rules]\n  Rules --> Commit[Transaction/batch or tracked job]\n  Commit --> Store[Canonical private records + derived projections]\n  Commit --> Outbox[Durable domain event/outbox]\n  Store --> Ack[Result ID/version + permitted next actions]\n  Ack --> Cache[Typed ID/query cache invalidation]\n  Cache --> Views[All affected authorized views]\n  Outbox --> Delivery[Tracked recipient notification delivery]\n```\n\n## Service responsibility\n\nRead projections may use Firebase directly when rules can enforce the full field/document scope. Membership, moderation propagation, sensitive cross-entity decisions, ID review/version checks, allowance accounting, recipient fanout and erasure need a trusted transaction/job contract. “Backend” denotes responsibility, not permission to add a new paid service. Existing SDK/Functions infrastructure may satisfy contracts once verified. Do not rely on hidden controls or client-supplied isAdmin/role fields.\n\nThe result includes command ID, entity ID/version, final or queued state, applicable retry/conflict information and a safe event reference. Known successful writes are not deleted because secondary notification delivery fails. An ambiguous timeout is reconciled by idempotency key before retrying. Multi-step Storage/Firestore work is not described as atomic; stage objects, commit references and clean abandoned state through tracked retention.\n\n## Field semantics\n\nUse typed money amounts/currency/unit; room share, full-property rent and per-bed price are not interchangeable. Preserve true zero deposit and computed zero match; absence is null/unknown rather than fabricated value. Dates have canonical timestamps/date/window types; display labels are derived, never persisted as “Today” or “Now” substitutes. Display names, legal/declared names, document types and review notes use explicit adapters. Account role labels do not grant publishing, residence or staff capability. Public/member projections are explicit allowlists, not raw account documents with four fields blanked in the UI.\n\n## Query/index and compatibility plan\n\nDefine supported city/locality/kind/publication/availability/price-unit predicates and stable order before index design. Query key and cursor include normalized filter/ranking versions. Supporting host/owner/entity lookups are bounded and counted. Entity-by-ID reads authorize independently of the discovery query. Per-conversation history and staff lists are paginated. Aggregate counters/trends declare their scope and retain zero instead of synthetic growth.\n\nProposed contract changes require field-version readers, explicit old→new adapters and test fixtures for every supported legacy shape. Inventory actual legacy data read-only before proposing a backfill. No role/intent/opt-in/residence/status is auto-inferred or mass-activated. A migration is a separate reviewed operation with dry run, backup, idempotency, rollback and postconditions; this blueprint grants no migration authority.\n\n## Input/output contract examples\n\n'+table(['Operation','Input','Acknowledged output','Critical invariant'],[
 ['ReadEntity','Typed ID + viewer/session + optional authorized context','Projection + version + available actions OR scoped unavailable/error','No feed position or context query grants access.'],
 ['SubmitInterest','Listing/version + answers + client command ID','Application ID + pair request state + usage result','No attributed application without listingId; no duplicate charge.'],
 ['DecideConsent','Request/version + recipient decision','Accepted/closed current version + event ID','Only current recipient decision; block/withdraw conflict wins safely.'],
 ['SendMessage','Room/clientMessageId + text/objectRef','Persisted message ID + room/read metadata version','Live authorization and idempotency at commit.'],
 ['ReviewEvidence','Submission/version + reviewer decision/reason','Decision/version + derived trust job/commit','Exact inspected version; no Aadhaar/property claims.'],
 ['ChangeAvailability','Listing/version + explicit capacity/status','Current availability/publication result','No fill from selection/consent.'],
 ['RequestErasure','Self recent auth + confirmation + approved scope','Owner job ID/status/retention summary','No false complete status or accidental peer-history deletion.']])+
 '\nThe actual implementation comparison is added only after the target model is defined; see the mapping appendix generated in this folder’s comparison phase.');

const events=[
 ['Search/filter changes','No domain write; normalized URL/query version.','Landing/Explore query/filter controls and cursor.','No recipient event.','New results only for latest query; related detail return context retained.'],
 ['Bookmark set/remove','Own typed bookmark/version.','Landing feature card, feed/detail save control, Saved.','None required.','Same desired saved state after reload; unavailable references remain removable.'],
 ['Intent/disclosure edit','Private profile + projection/eligibility version.','Own profile/preferences, people detail, directory, publisher contextual profile.','Only necessary policy/security confirmation.','Revoke visibility promptly; existing authorized private contexts remain separately scoped.'],
 ['Listing submitted/reviewed','Draft/review version + publication projection/job.','My listings/wizard, staff queue, public detail/feed, Saved.','Publisher review status and reviewer work queue.','No pending-as-active mapping or publication from identity approval alone.'],
 ['Availability filled/expired/restricted','Availability + effective published projection.','Every discovery section, shared link, Saved, chat context, applicants and resident host eligibility.','Relevant applicant/publisher status without spam or false tenancy.','No new inquiry; honest history/tombstone; other independent personal intents survive.'],
 ['Listing interest submitted','Application/answer snapshot + needed consent/usage event.','Applicant own status, publisher Applicants, Connections, person/property actions.','Publisher receives attributed interest/request.','Existing accepted pair reuses consent; questions/answers retained privately.'],
 ['Consent accepted/declined/withdrawn','Pair request version + authorization mirror.','Cards/person/detail/Connections/Notifications/chat composer.','Other participant receives minimal current result.','Same enabled action everywhere; no property fill or applicant selection.'],
 ['Message acknowledged/read','Message/summary + per-member read state.','Both room streams, room list, unread filter/badges, permitted notifications.','Actual delivery tracked separately.','Draft transitions to acknowledged by ID; read counts do not regress from stale snapshots.'],
 ['Block/unblock','Directional block + effective pair access.','All pair contexts, existing/new chat, attachments, own restricted list and request controls.','Do not notify peer who blocked or why.','Restriction persists across IDs; removing own block does not auto-accept.'],
 ['Applicant stage change','Listing-scoped application version/note.','Owner applicant/compare/detail and applicant status.','Relevant consideration update, not a tenancy contract.','No implicit request acceptance or filled listing.'],
 ['ID decision','Exact submission decision + trust projection/version.','Owner verification/profile, publisher prerequisites, staff queue and public badge where applicable.','Owner sees true decision/reason.','No public evidence URL, government certification or property auto-activation.'],
 ['Sanction/reinstatement','Account moderation + publication/send eligibility/job.','Member restriction/support, directory, properties, conversations, staff case.','Policy-appropriate member notice.','Server paths agree; reinstatement rechecks prerequisites, not blanket active.'],
 ['Report resolution','Case outcome/note + required action job.','Staff queues/inspector, target state and safe reporter acknowledgement.','Actual case result, avoiding private staff/evidence disclosure.','Resolved only after required action applies or explicit no-action decision.'],
 ['Outcome declared/corrected','Private outcome + explicitly chosen intent changes.','Own outcome/profile/search preferences; host prompt if relevant.','Optional follow-up only.','No peer occupancy or listing fill unless publisher separately confirms.'],
 ['Export/deletion/broadcast','Job manifest and delivery/erasure progress.','Owner/staff job status, actual completed scope and relevant caches.','Only real acknowledgements/deliveries.','Retry resumes job ID; no fake success after partial failure.'],
];
write('CROSS_PAGE_CONSISTENCY_MAP','Cross-page consistency map',
 '## Event contract\n\nA single domain event carries ID, actor, typed entity/version, effective time, required consumers and disclosure scope. Commit authoritative state first; deliver notifications/propagate projections through an idempotent outbox/job where the operation cannot be atomic. A consumer displays pending propagation explicitly rather than contradictory final states. Private cache keys include account UID and authorization version; sign-out/revocation invalidates them.\n\n'+table(['Business event','Records changing','Pages that must update','Notification obligation','Availability/cache/refresh invariant'],events)+
 '\n## Cross-page acceptance scenarios\n\n- Send one request from a person card: the same target detail, listing context, Sent tab and recipient Incoming show one pending ID; duplicate/reverse requests do not create a second charge.\n- Accept on recipient notification: sender profile/card offers Message; recipient application remains its own consideration stage; listing capacity is unchanged.\n- Block inside an old room: new text/attachment commits and fresh-ID requests fail, every composer/action becomes restricted, permitted history remains truthful.\n- Fill a listing outside the app: every public query/shared link shows the right state; have_room-only availability disappears; concurrent team_up may remain.\n- Edit a bio after choosing three localities: unchanged locality preferences remain on all profile/preference/discovery views.\n- Review an ID while another reviewer acts: a version conflict cannot approve an unseen new submission; staff/owner/public badge agree on the applied decision.\n- Suspend a publisher: existing property cards and direct entry stop accepting new inquiries; the staff case is not marked completed before restriction propagation.\n- Delete or lose access to a saved person: Saved shows a removable scoped unavailable item; it does not silently lose the bookmark or reveal private existence.\n\nEach scenario must be checked after reload and from every involved actor’s independent session, not just with a local visual update.');

const failures=[
 ['Cancel/Back/Close','UI draft or committed state known.','Before commit, no successful business event. Save draft and Discard are explicit alternatives. After commit, reverse through a separate domain command.','Preserve safe origin context; clear sensitive transient bytes; do not publish an avatar from an abandoned edit.'],
 ['Refresh/direct link','Typed ID/query and authorized scope exist.','Re-fetch current entity/version independently; resume only owned safe drafts/jobs.','Unknown target and network failure are distinct; never rely on previously loaded cards.'],
 ['Session expiry/account switch','Auth token expired or another UID signs in.','Freeze writes; clear/rekey private cache; preserve only scoped nonsensitive intended action.','Reauthenticate then reauthorize/review before resubmitting; never auto-send another user’s draft.'],
 ['Offline/backend failure','Command not acknowledged or outcome ambiguous.','Maintain failed/pending local draft, not success; show network state.','Reconcile by idempotency key before retry; do not duplicate requests, charges, messages or jobs.'],
 ['Double click/retry','Same logical command may arrive more than once.','Disable accidental duplicate UI submission and enforce server idempotency.','Same command ID returns same result; UI mutex alone is insufficient.'],
 ['Simultaneous accept/withdraw/block','Expected version no longer current.','Atomic version/precondition check chooses valid current transition; block overrides sends.','Refresh actual state and explain conflict; never last-write-wins consent against a block.'],
 ['Concurrent listing/profile edit','Another actor/version changed relevant fields.','Compare explicit diff/current version; do not overwrite undisplayed fields or approval.','Offer reload/merge owned edits; material changes require review policy.'],
 ['Listing fills/pauses while viewed','A formerly available place changes.','Read current effective availability before inquiry commit; invalidate relevant context/actions.','Preserve draft answers but require review of changed listing; provide another search, not fake success.'],
 ['Account suspended/banned','Member or counterpart becomes restricted.','Enforce publication/send/request denial on server, including already-open views.','Show scoped restriction/support; keep approved data-rights/history access separate.'],
 ['Upload fails/cancels','Owned staging object/draft exists.','No final reference or message success without validated object; no base64 bypass.','Retry same upload/command; clean orphans by manifest/expiry with safe retry.'],
 ['Verification rejected/raced','A submission has actual reason/version or another reviewer changes it.','Owner sees real type/name/note; resubmits a new version. Reviewer may only decide inspected version.','No user self-approval; retain/revoke/clean evidence per approved schedule.'],
 ['Related record missing/private/deleted','Entity resolver returns scoped unavailable or service error.','Use an honest unavailable projection/tombstone, not invented owner, rent, location or identity.','Allow safe removal/retry/back; preserve authorized context without leaking private existence.'],
 ['Notification delivery fails','Domain commit already succeeded.','Keep domain result; queue/retry delivery independently with idempotent recipient events.','Display sent/queued/delivered states honestly; no compensating deletion of a committed request.'],
 ['Partial sanction/erasure/broadcast','Only some manifest work succeeded.','Track applying/partially failed and exact completed scope; avoid final resolved/deleted/delivered claim.','Resume trusted job; retain necessary identity/authorization until retry is safe; honor retention exceptions explicitly.'],
 ['Quota exceeded/renewed','Period/usage policy returned by server.','Show actual remaining/renewal or supported recovery; no absent upgrade link.','No silent refunds, reset, old-counter reinterpretation or duplicate consumption; migration separately reviewed.'],
 ['Legacy ID/data shape','Old paths/fields differ from the target.','Use a reviewed explicit adapter or request supported resubmission; never open arbitrary active content.','Do not migrate on read/login; inventory/dry-run/backup/approval precedes legacy changes.'],
 ['Permission/clipboard/provider denial','Browser/API refuses a secondary operation.','No success before its actual promise/result; preserve primary domain state.','Offer copyable text, provider-specific recovery or clear unsupported message; do not swallow async rejection.'],
];
write('FAILURE_AND_RECOVERY_WORKFLOWS','Failure and recovery workflows',
 '## Recovery contract\n\nEvery read distinguishes loading, known empty, forbidden/unavailable and failure. Every write distinguishes local draft, pending/queued, acknowledged, conflict and failed/partially failed. An optimistic visual change is never the sole proof of success. Sensitive commands carry actor, idempotency key and expected version; secondary operations use tracked jobs/events. No recovery path bypasses authorization or silently changes another lifecycle.\n\n'+table(['Failure / edge case','Trigger/precondition','Expected behavior','Recovery / durable result'],failures)+
 '\n## Failure sequence\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n  participant U as User\n  participant UI as View/draft\n  participant S as Authorized service\n  participant DB as State store\n  U->>UI: Submit explicit command\n  UI->>S: Actor + commandId + expectedVersion\n  S->>DB: Authorize and commit if current\n  DB-->>S: Result or conflict\n  S--xUI: Response lost\n  UI-->>U: Outcome unknown; draft retained\n  U->>UI: Retry\n  UI->>S: Reconcile same commandId\n  S->>DB: Read prior command result\n  DB-->>S: Existing acknowledged result\n  S-->>UI: Same entity/version, no duplicate charge\n  UI-->>U: Confirmed result + valid next action\n```\n\n## Required resilience acceptance\n\nFor each T01–T32 command, test cancellation before/after acknowledgement, reload, stale response, repeat command, auth switch, offline/permission failure and any relevant competing actor. Test model actions on independent sessions and inspect authoritative writes, not just toasts. Explicitly test source-created-but-not-yet-uploaded drafts, successful upload but failed reference commit, ID rejection/resubmission while review is open, existing chat after block, saved records outside discovery, and case resolution when its sanction fails.\n\nNever broaden Firestore/Storage rules to hide a client error. Never restore old permissive behavior during rollback without a reviewed compatibility/security decision. A missing provider or unapproved product policy is marked blocked/unavailable with a clear next step, not invented implementation.');

